module

public import Mathlib
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.CechNerveHomology
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Cohomology of a chaotic site with a covering object

Let `𝒞` be a small category carrying the *chaotic* topology, the one whose only coverings are the
singleton isomorphisms, so that every presheaf is a sheaf ([Stacks, Tag 07GE]); it is the bottom
Grothendieck topology `⊥`. Let `X` be an object of `𝒞` such that every object of `𝒞` has a
morphism towards `X`, and assume the nonempty finite powers `X^{n + 1}` of `X` exist in `𝒞`. Then
for every abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `𝒞` the total cohomology `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` is represented by the complex

```
𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯
```

associated to the cosimplicial abelian group `[n] ↦ 𝓕(X^{n + 1})`. This is [Stacks, Tag 07JM].

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.powerSimplicial`: the simplicial object `[n] ↦ X^{n + 1}` of nonempty finite
  powers of `X`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.powerCechComplex`: the complex `𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → ⋯` associated to the
  cosimplicial abelian group of the values of `𝓕` on those powers.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.evSheaf`, `Stacks.Cohomology.freeYonedaSectionsIso`: maps out of the free
  abelian sheaf generated by `h_U` are the sections over `U`, naturally in `U`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.chaoticResolution`: the resolution of the constant abelian sheaf `ℤ` by the
  free abelian sheaves on the powers of `X`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.chaoticDerivedGlobalSections`: `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)`, the `Hom`-complex out of that
  resolution, which is K-projective.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.projective_freeAbelianSheaf_yoneda`: on the chaotic site the free abelian
  sheaf generated by a representable presheaf of sets is projective, sections over an object
  being an exact functor there.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend`: **[Stacks, Tag 07JM]**,
  `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` is isomorphic, as a complex of abelian groups, to the complex of the values of `𝓕`
  on the powers of `X` placed in the nonnegative degrees.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.derivedGlobalSectionsQIsoPowerCechComplexExtend`: **[Stacks, Tag 07JM]** in
  `D(Ab)`, the same comparison read in the derived category of abelian groups.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.sheafHAddEquivPowerCechComplexHomology`,
  `Stacks.Cohomology.functorHObjIsoPowerCechComplexHomology`: the comparison in degree `n`, the
  named isomorphism of `H^n(𝒞, 𝓕)` with the degree-`n` cohomology of that complex, as an
  isomorphism of abelian groups and as one of objects of `AddCommGrpCat`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.addEquivSheafHHomologyPowerCechComplex`: **[Stacks, Tag 07JM] with its
  comparison named**, the isomorphism of `H^n(𝒞, 𝓕)` with the degree-`n` cohomology of the
  complex of the values of `𝓕` on the powers of `X`, as a `def` rather than an existence
  statement.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.nonempty_addEquiv_sheafH_homology_powerCechComplex`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 07JM]**, the cohomology of `𝓕` in every degree is the cohomology of the complex
  of the values of `𝓕` on the powers of `X`.  It is the previous one read as an existence
  statement.

## Implementation notes

Cohomology of the site is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H`, the `Ext`-groups out of the
constant abelian sheaf `ℤ`; that these are the right derived functors of global sections is
`Stacks.Cohomology.SiteSections.functorHIsoRightDerivedSiteSections`. Global sections over a site
are `Mor(ℤ, -)` out of that constant sheaf, so `RΓ(𝒞, -)` is `RHom(ℤ, -)`, and it is realized
here as the `Hom`-complex out of the K-projective resolution
`Stacks.Cohomology.chaoticResolution` (Mathlib's `IsKProjective` instance on the cochain
complex of a projective resolution).
"Represented by the complex" is therefore an isomorphism of complexes of abelian groups, hence an
isomorphism in `D(Ab)`; the degreewise statement about `H^n(𝒞, 𝓕)` is its `H^n`.

The source deduces the lemma from [Stacks, Tag 079Z], the Čech spectral sequence of the
surjection `h_X → *`. That route is not taken here: the library's form of 079Z
(`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence`) produces a spectral
sequence whose first page has the right terms but whose differentials are not identified, so it
cannot yield the cohomology of one named complex. Instead the resolution 079Z is proved from is
used directly. The free abelian sheaves on the terms of the Čech nerve of `h_X → *` form a
resolution of the free abelian sheaf on `*` — this is [Stacks, Tag 01GC],
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.quasiIso_cechNerveSheafAugmentation`, whose hypothesis holds because
every object of `𝒞` has a morphism to `X` — and on the chaotic site those sheaves are
*projective*, because sections over an object of the site are an exact functor there. So the Čech
nerve is a projective resolution, and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.ProjectiveResolution.extAddEquivCohomologyClass` computes `Ext` out of the
constant sheaf as the cohomology of the `Hom`-complex of that resolution. The terms of the Čech
nerve are the powers of `X`, by `CategoryTheory.CechNerveTerminalFrom.iso` together with the fact
that Yoneda preserves products, so the `Hom`-complex is the complex of the statement.

The source asks `𝒞` to have products of pairs, and the hypothesis carried here is weaker: only
the powers `X^{n + 1}` of the covering object are ever formed, so the hypothesis is literally
`∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)` and nothing is assumed about products of
distinct objects. The source's hypothesis implies it, by
`Stacks.Cohomology.hasProduct_fin_succ`, which is the bridge a site with all products of pairs
uses. The weaker form is what lets the engine run on sites where only the powers of one chosen
object are known to exist — for instance the completed affine crystalline site, where the powers
of the generator are the objects `D(n)` of [Stacks, Tag 07L4] and coproducts of arbitrary pairs
are not available. No terminal object of `𝒞` is assumed, in accordance with the source. The
terminal object used is the terminal presheaf of sets, which always exists.

The `Hom`-complex of Mathlib is indexed by `ℤ` and its differential carries the sign `(-1)^{n+1}`
of the cochain differential `δ`, whereas the complex associated to a cosimplicial abelian group is
indexed by `ℕ` with the alternating sum of the cofaces as differential. The two are matched by
`Stacks.Cohomology.cochainToHomEquiv`, which folds the compensating sign `(-1)^{n(n+1)/2}` into
the degreewise identification, and by extension by zero along `ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01GC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01GC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07GE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07GE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 079Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07L4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicTopology
open CochainComplex.HomComplex

universe w u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

/-! ### Generalities -/

section General

/-- Precomposition along an isomorphism, as an isomorphism of groups of homomorphisms. -/
def precompAddEquiv {A : Type*} [Category* A] [Preadditive A] {P Q F : A} (i : P ≅ Q) :
    (P ⟶ F) ≃+ (Q ⟶ F) where
  toFun f := i.inv ≫ f
  invFun g := i.hom ≫ g
  left_inv f := by simp
  right_inv g := by simp
  map_add' _ _ := by simp

/-- The sign `(-1)^{n(n+1)/2}`, written by recursion. -/
def altSign : ℕ → ℤˣ
  | 0 => 1
  | (n + 1) => ((n + 1 : ℤ)).negOnePow * altSign n

/-- The recursion defining the signs. -/
lemma altSign_succ (n : ℕ) : altSign (n + 1) = ((n + 1 : ℤ)).negOnePow * altSign n := rfl

variable {A : Type*} [Category* A] [Abelian A]

/-- Degree-`n` cochains into a complex concentrated in degree zero are the maps out of the
degree-`(-n)` term, up to a sign. -/
def cochainToHomEquiv {K : CochainComplex A ℤ} {R : ChainComplex A ℕ}
    (ι : ∀ (n : ℕ), K.X (-(n : ℤ)) ≅ R.X n) (F : A) (n : ℕ) :
    Cochain K ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor A 0).obj F) (n : ℤ) ≃+ (R.X n ⟶ F) :=
  ((Cochain.toSingleEquiv (K := K) (X := F) (p := -(n : ℤ)) (q := 0) (n := (n : ℤ))
      (by simp)).trans (precompAddEquiv (ι n))).trans
    (DistribMulAction.toAddEquiv _ (altSign n))

/-- The value of `Stacks.Cohomology.cochainToHomEquiv` on a cochain written through
`CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.toSingleMk`. -/
lemma cochainToHomEquiv_apply {K : CochainComplex A ℤ} {R : ChainComplex A ℕ}
    (ι : ∀ (n : ℕ), K.X (-(n : ℤ)) ≅ R.X n) (F : A) (n : ℕ) (f : K.X (-(n : ℤ)) ⟶ F)
    (h : -(n : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) = 0) :
    cochainToHomEquiv ι F n (Cochain.toSingleMk f h) = altSign n • ((ι n).inv ≫ f) := by
  simp [cochainToHomEquiv, precompAddEquiv]

/-- Under the identification of cochains into a single complex with maps out of the terms, the
differential of the `Hom`-complex becomes precomposition with the differential. -/
lemma cochainToHomEquiv_delta {K : CochainComplex A ℤ} {R : ChainComplex A ℕ}
    (ι : ∀ (n : ℕ), K.X (-(n : ℤ)) ≅ R.X n)
    (hd : ∀ n : ℕ, (ι (n + 1)).inv ≫ K.d (-((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (-(n : ℤ)) =
      R.d (n + 1) n ≫ (ι n).inv)
    (F : A) (n : ℕ) (z : Cochain K ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor A 0).obj F) (n : ℤ)) :
    cochainToHomEquiv ι F (n + 1) (δ (n : ℤ) ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) z) =
      R.d (n + 1) n ≫ cochainToHomEquiv ι F n z := by
  obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := Cochain.toSingleMk_surjective z (-(n : ℤ)) (by simp)
  have hs : ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ).negOnePow * altSign (n + 1) = altSign n := by
    rw [altSign_succ]
    push_cast
    rw [← mul_assoc, Int.units_mul_self, one_mul]
  rw [Cochain.δ_toSingleMk _ _ (((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (-((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (by push_cast; ring),
    Units.smul_def, map_zsmul, ← Units.smul_def, cochainToHomEquiv_apply,
    cochainToHomEquiv_apply, smul_smul, hs, ← Category.assoc, hd n, Category.assoc]
  simp [Units.smul_def]

/-- Cochains of negative degree into a complex concentrated in degree zero, out of a complex
concentrated in the nonpositive degrees, vanish. -/
lemma isZero_homComplex_X {K : CochainComplex A ℤ} [K.IsStrictlyLE 0]
    (F : A) (q : ℤ) (hq : q < 0) :
    IsZero ((K.HomComplex ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor A 0).obj F)).X q) := by
  have h0 : IsZero (K.X (-q)) := K.isZero_of_isStrictlyLE 0 (-q) (by lia)
  have h1 : Subsingleton (K.X (-q) ⟶ F) := ⟨fun a b => h0.eq_of_src a b⟩
  have h2 : Subsingleton (Cochain K ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor A 0).obj F) q) :=
    (Cochain.toSingleEquiv (K := K) (X := F) (p := -q) (q := 0) (n := q)
      (by ring)).injective.subsingleton
  exact @AddCommGrpCat.isZero_of_subsingleton _ h2

/-- An alternating coface complex built from an additive contravariant functor has the expected
differential. -/
lemma alternatingCofaceMapComplex_d {B : Type*} [Category* B] [Preadditive B]
    {A' : Type*} [Category* A'] [Preadditive A'] (G : A'ᵒᵖ ⥤ B) [G.Additive]
    (Y : SimplicialObject A') (n : ℕ) :
    ((alternatingCofaceMapComplex B).obj (Y.rightOp ⋙ G)).d n (n + 1) =
      G.map (((alternatingFaceMapComplex A').obj Y).d (n + 1) n).op := by
  rw [alternatingFaceMapComplex_obj_d]
  dsimp [alternatingCofaceMapComplex, AlternatingCofaceMapComplex.obj]
  rw [CochainComplex.of_d]
  dsimp [AlternatingCofaceMapComplex.objD, AlternatingFaceMapComplex.objD]
  rw [op_sum, G.map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [op_zsmul, G.map_zsmul]
  rfl

end General

end Stacks.Cohomology

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

/-! ### Powers of an object -/

section Powers
variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]

/-- A category with products of pairs has products of every nonempty finite family. In particular
it has the powers `X^{n + 1}` that the constructions below form, which is the only way the
hypothesis of the source is used here. -/
lemma hasProduct_fin_succ [HasBinaryProducts C] : ∀ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin (n + 1) → C), HasProduct f
  | 0 => fun _ => by
      have : Unique (Fin (0 + 1)) := inferInstanceAs (Unique (Fin 1))
      infer_instance
  | (n + 1) => fun f => by
      have := hasProduct_fin_succ n (fun i : Fin (n + 1) => f i.succ)
      exact HasLimit.mk ⟨_, extendFanIsLimit f (limit.isLimit _) (limit.isLimit _)⟩

/-- The simplicial object `[n] ↦ X^{n+1}` of nonempty finite powers of an object `X`. Only the
powers of `X` itself are assumed to exist; no products of distinct objects are formed. -/
def powerSimplicial (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)] :
    SimplicialObject C where
  obj n := ∏ᶜ (fun _ : Fin (n.unop.len + 1) => X)
  map g := Pi.lift (fun i => Pi.π _ (g.unop.toOrderHom i))
  map_id _ := Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun _ => by simp
  map_comp _ _ := Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun _ => by simp

/-- The Yoneda embedding carries the powers of `X` to the powers of `h_X`. -/
def powerSimplicialCompYonedaIso (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)] :
    powerSimplicial X ⋙ yoneda ≅ cechNerveTerminalFrom (yoneda.obj X) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun n => PreservesProduct.iso yoneda _) (by
    intro m n g
    apply Pi.hom_ext
    intro j
    dsimp [powerSimplicial, cechNerveTerminalFrom]
    simp)

/-- The Čech nerve of `h_X → *` is the simplicial object of powers of `X`. -/
def cechNerveIso (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)] :
    (Arrow.mk (terminal.from (yoneda.obj X))).cechNerve ≅ powerSimplicial X ⋙ yoneda :=
  CechNerveTerminalFrom.iso (yoneda.obj X) ≪≫ (powerSimplicialCompYonedaIso X).symm

/-- The complex `𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯` associated to the cosimplicial abelian
group `[n] ↦ 𝓕(X^{n+1})` of the values of an abelian presheaf on the powers of `X`. -/
def powerCechComplex (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u}) (X : C)
    [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)] :
    CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u} ℕ :=
  (alternatingCofaceMapComplex _).obj ((powerSimplicial X).rightOp ⋙ F)

/-- Degree `n` of the complex of the values of `𝓕` on the powers of `X` is `𝓕(X^{n + 1})`. -/
lemma powerCechComplex_X (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u}) (X : C)
    [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)] (n : ℕ) :
    (powerCechComplex F X).X n = F.obj (op (∏ᶜ (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X))) := rfl

end Powers

/-! ### Sections as maps out of a free abelian sheaf -/

section Ev
variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]
variable (J : GrothendieckTopology C) [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- Maps out of the free abelian sheaf on `h_U` are the sections over `U`. -/
def evSheaf (U : C) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U) ⟶ F) ≃ F.obj.obj (op U) :=
  ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheafAdj J).homEquiv (yoneda.obj U) F).trans yonedaEquiv

/-- The tautological section over `U` of the free abelian sheaf on `h_U`. -/
def tautSection (U : C) :
    ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U)).obj.obj (op U) :=
  (((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheafAdj J).unit.app (yoneda.obj U)).app (op U)) (𝟙 U)

/-- The bijection `Stacks.Cohomology.evSheaf` evaluates a map at the tautological section. -/
lemma evSheaf_apply (U : C) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (φ : (Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U) ⟶ F) :
    evSheaf J U F φ = φ.hom.app (op U) (tautSection J U) := by
  rw [evSheaf, Equiv.trans_apply, yonedaEquiv_apply, Adjunction.homEquiv_unit]
  rfl

/-- `Stacks.Cohomology.evSheaf` is natural in the object of the site. -/
lemma evSheaf_naturality_left (U V : C) (h : U ⟶ V) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (φ : (Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj V) ⟶ F) :
    evSheaf J U F ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).map (yoneda.map h) ≫ φ) =
      F.obj.map h.op (evSheaf J V F φ) := by
  rw [evSheaf, evSheaf, Equiv.trans_apply, Equiv.trans_apply,
    Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left, ← yonedaEquiv_naturality]
  rfl

/-- `Stacks.Cohomology.evSheaf` is natural in the sheaf. -/
lemma evSheaf_naturality_right (U : C) {F G : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}} (p : F ⟶ G)
    (φ : (Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U) ⟶ F) :
    evSheaf J U G (φ ≫ p) = p.hom.app (op U) (evSheaf J U F φ) := by
  rw [evSheaf_apply, evSheaf_apply]
  rfl

/-- `Stacks.Cohomology.evSheaf` is additive. -/
lemma evSheaf_add (U : C) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (φ ψ : (Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U) ⟶ F) :
    evSheaf J U F (φ + ψ) = evSheaf J U F φ + evSheaf J U F ψ := by
  rw [evSheaf_apply, evSheaf_apply, evSheaf_apply]
  simp

/-- `evSheaf` as an isomorphism of abelian groups. -/
def evSheafAddEquiv (U : C) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (yoneda.obj U) ⟶ F) ≃+ F.obj.obj (op U) :=
  AddEquiv.mk' (evSheaf J U F) (evSheaf_add J U F)

/-- The sections of an abelian sheaf are the maps out of the free abelian sheaves generated by
the representable presheaves of sets. -/
def freeYonedaSectionsIso (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    (yoneda ⋙ Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).op ⋙ preadditiveYoneda.obj F ≅ F.obj :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun U => (evSheafAddEquiv J U.unop F).toAddCommGrpIso) (by
    intro U V g
    ext φ
    exact evSheaf_naturality_left J V.unop U.unop g.unop F φ)

end Ev

/-! ### The chaotic topology -/

section Chaotic
variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]

/-- The sections of the terminal presheaf of sets over any object form a singleton. -/
instance uniqueTerminalPresheafSections (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Unique ((⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)).obj U) :=
  have : Unique (yoneda.obj U.unop ⟶ (⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u))) := uniqueToTerminal _
  Equiv.unique (yonedaEquiv (X := U.unop) (F := ⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u))).symm

/-- The terminal presheaf of sets is the constant presheaf on a point. -/
def terminalPresheafIso :
    (⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)) ≅ (Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj PUnit.{u + 1} :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun U => (Equiv.equivPUnit.{u+1} ((⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)).obj U)).toIso)
    fun _ => Types.isTerminalPUnit.hom_ext _ _

/-- The free abelian presheaf on the terminal presheaf of sets is the constant presheaf `ℤ`. -/
def freeAbelianTerminalIso :
    (Presheaf.freeAbelian.obj (⊤_ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u}) ≅
      (Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj (AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)) :=
  Functor.isoWhiskerRight terminalPresheafIso AddCommGrpCat.free ≪≫
    Functor.constComp _ _ _ ≪≫
    (Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).mapIso
      ((FreeAbelianGroup.uniqueEquiv PUnit.{u + 1}).trans
        (AddEquiv.ulift : ULift.{u} ℤ ≃+ ℤ).symm).toAddCommGrpIso

/-- If every object of `C` has a morphism to `X`, the map `h_X → *` is locally surjective. -/
lemma isLocallySurjective_terminalFrom (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (X : C)
    (hX : ∀ U : C, Nonempty (U ⟶ X)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (terminal.from (yoneda.obj X)) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective _ _
    (fun U _ => ⟨(hX U.unop).some, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩)

/-- On the chaotic site an epimorphism of abelian sheaves is surjective on sections. -/
lemma surjective_app_of_epi {E Y : Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u}}
    (e : E ⟶ Y) [Epi e] (U : C) :
    Function.Surjective (ConcreteCategory.hom (e.hom.app (op U))) := by
  have h0 : (sheafToPresheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u}).PreservesEpimorphisms :=
    inferInstanceAs (sheafBotEquivalence (C := C) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).functor.PreservesEpimorphisms
  have h1 := h0.preserves e
  rw [NatTrans.epi_iff_epi_app] at h1
  have h2 := h1 (op U)
  rwa [AddCommGrpCat.epi_iff_surjective] at h2

/-- On the chaotic site the free abelian sheaf generated by a representable presheaf of sets is
projective. -/
lemma projective_freeAbelianSheaf_yoneda (U : C) :
    Projective ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)).obj (yoneda.obj U)) := by
  constructor
  intro E Y f e he
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := surjective_app_of_epi e U (evSheaf ⊥ U Y f)
  refine ⟨(evSheaf ⊥ U E).symm a, ?_⟩
  apply (evSheaf ⊥ U Y).injective
  rwa [evSheaf_naturality_right, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

end Chaotic

end Stacks.Cohomology

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

/-! ### Cohomology of a chaotic site with a covering object -/

section Main

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]
  (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)]
  (hX : ∀ U : C, Nonempty (U ⟶ X))
  (F : Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/-- The Čech nerve of `h_X → *` resolves the constant abelian sheaf `ℤ` by free abelian
sheaves on the powers of `X`, which are projective on the chaotic site. -/
def chaoticResolution :
    ProjectiveResolution ((constantSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))) where
  complex := (SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)).obj
    (powerSimplicial X ⋙ yoneda)
  projective _ := projective_freeAbelianSheaf_yoneda _
  π := (SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor
        (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)).map (cechNerveIso X).inv ≫
      Presheaf.cechNerveSheafAugmentation (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)
        (terminal.from (yoneda.obj X)) ≫
      (ChainComplex.single₀ _).map
        ((presheafToSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
          freeAbelianTerminalIso).hom
  quasiIso := by
    have h1 : QuasiIso (Presheaf.cechNerveSheafAugmentation (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)
        (terminal.from (yoneda.obj X))) :=
      Presheaf.quasiIso_cechNerveSheafAugmentation _ _
        (isLocallySurjective_terminalFrom _ X hX)
    have h2 : QuasiIso ((ChainComplex.single₀ (Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)
        AddCommGrpCat.{u})).map
        ((presheafToSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
          freeAbelianTerminalIso).hom) := quasiIso_of_isIso _
    have h3 : QuasiIso ((SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor
        (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)).map (cechNerveIso X).inv) := quasiIso_of_isIso _
    exact quasiIso_comp _ _ (hφ := h3)
      (hφ' := quasiIso_comp _ _ (hφ := h1) (hφ' := h2))

/-- The complex of maps out of the terms of `Stacks.Cohomology.chaoticResolution`. -/
def powerFreeCechComplex : CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u} ℕ :=
  (alternatingCofaceMapComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
    ((powerSimplicial X ⋙ yoneda ⋙
      Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C)).rightOp ⋙
      preadditiveYoneda.obj F)

/-- The complex of the values of `𝓕` on the powers of `X` is the complex of maps out of the
terms of the resolution. -/
def powerCechComplexIso : powerCechComplex F.obj X ≅ powerFreeCechComplex X F :=
  (alternatingCofaceMapComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
    (Functor.isoWhiskerLeft ((powerSimplicial X).rightOp)
      (freeYonedaSectionsIso (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) F).symm)

end Main

end Stacks.Cohomology

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

section Main2

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]
  (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)]
  (hX : ∀ U : C, Nonempty (U ⟶ X))
  (F : Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/-- The isomorphisms identifying the terms of the extended resolution. -/
def resXIso (m : ℕ) :
    (chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex.X (-(m : ℤ)) ≅
      (chaoticResolution X hX).complex.X m :=
  (chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplexXIso (-(m : ℤ)) m rfl

/-- The identifications of the terms of the extended resolution carry its differential to the
differential of the resolution. -/
lemma resXIso_d (n : ℕ) :
    (resXIso X hX (n + 1)).inv ≫ (chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex.d
        (-((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (-(n : ℤ)) =
      (chaoticResolution X hX).complex.d (n + 1) n ≫ (resXIso X hX n).inv := by
  rw [(chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex_d (-((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (-(n : ℤ)) (n + 1) n,
    ← Category.assoc]
  simp [resXIso]

/-- Degree `n` of the comparison of the `Hom`-complex of the resolution with the complex of the
values of `𝓕` on the powers of `X`. -/
def cechPhiIso (n : ℕ) :
    ((((chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex).HomComplex
        ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor _ 0).obj F)).restriction
      ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat).X n ≅ (powerFreeCechComplex X F).X n :=
  (cochainToHomEquiv (resXIso X hX) F n).toAddCommGrpIso

/-- The comparison of the `Hom`-complex of the resolution with the complex of the values of
`𝓕` on the powers of `X`. -/
def cechPhi :
    (((chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex).HomComplex
        ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor _ 0).obj F)).restriction
      ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat ⟶ powerFreeCechComplex X F where
  f n := (cechPhiIso X hX F n).hom
  comm' n m hnm := by
    obtain rfl : n + 1 = m := hnm
    rw [show (powerFreeCechComplex X F).d n (n + 1) =
        (preadditiveYoneda.obj F).map
          (((alternatingFaceMapComplex _).obj (powerSimplicial X ⋙ yoneda ⋙
            Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C))).d (n + 1) n).op from
      alternatingCofaceMapComplex_d _ _ n]
    ext z
    exact (cochainToHomEquiv_delta (resXIso X hX) (resXIso_d X hX) F n z).symm

end Main2

end Stacks.Cohomology

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

section Main3

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]
  (X : C) [∀ n : ℕ, HasProduct (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => X)]
  (hX : ∀ U : C, Nonempty (U ⟶ X))
  (F : Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/-- The components of `Stacks.Cohomology.cechPhi`. -/
lemma cechPhi_f (n : ℕ) : (cechPhi X hX F).f n = (cechPhiIso X hX F n).hom := rfl

/-- The comparison extends by zero to the negative degrees. -/
lemma cechPhi_hasLift : ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.HasLift (cechPhi X hX F) := by
  intro j hj i' hij
  obtain rfl : j = 0 := by
    rcases j with _ | k
    · rfl
    · exact absurd hj (ComplexShape.Embedding.not_boundaryGE_next
        (e := ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat) (j := k) (k := k + 1) rfl)
  obtain rfl : i' = -1 := by
    have : i' + 1 = ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ) := hij
    lia
  exact (isZero_homComplex_X F (-1) (by lia)).eq_of_src _ _

/-- The extended comparison is an isomorphism of complexes. -/
lemma isIso_cechPhi_liftExtend :
    IsIso (ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.liftExtend (cechPhi X hX F) (cechPhi_hasLift X hX F)) := by
  have h : ∀ (i' : ℤ), IsIso ((ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.liftExtend (cechPhi X hX F)
      (cechPhi_hasLift X hX F)).f i') := by
    intro i'
    rcases le_or_gt 0 i' with hi | hi
    · obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le hi
      refine (ComplexShape.Embedding.isIso_liftExtend_f_iff _ _ _ (i := n) rfl).2 ?_
      rw [cechPhi_f]
      exact (cechPhiIso X hX F n).isIso_hom
    · have hA := isZero_homComplex_X (K := (chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex) F i' hi
      have hB := HomologicalComplex.isZero_extend_X (powerFreeCechComplex X F)
        ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat i' (fun k hk => by
          rw [show ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.f k = (k : ℤ) from rfl] at hk
          omega)
      exact ⟨0, hA.eq_of_src _ _, hB.eq_of_tgt _ _⟩
  exact @HomologicalComplex.Hom.isIso_of_components _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ h

/-- The `Hom`-complex of the resolution is the complex of the values of `𝓕` on the powers of
`X`, placed in the nonnegative degrees. -/
def homComplexExtendIso :
    ((chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex).HomComplex
        ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor _ 0).obj F) ≅
      (powerFreeCechComplex X F).extend ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat :=
  have := isIso_cechPhi_liftExtend X hX F
  asIso (ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.liftExtend (cechPhi X hX F) (cechPhi_hasLift X hX F))

/-- `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)`, the derived global sections of an abelian sheaf on the chaotic site, realized as
the `Hom`-complex out of the resolution `Stacks.Cohomology.chaoticResolution` of the constant
abelian sheaf `ℤ`.

Global sections over a site are `Mor(ℤ, -)` out of the constant abelian sheaf `ℤ`, so
`RΓ(𝒞, -)` is `RHom(ℤ, -)`, and the `Hom`-complex out of a K-projective resolution of the source
computes it. The resolution used is K-projective, by Mathlib's `IsKProjective` instance on the
cochain complex of a projective resolution, which is what makes this complex the object
`RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` rather than just one complex computing its cohomology groups; the cohomology of this
complex in degree `n` is `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H 𝓕 n`, the `Ext`-group Mathlib takes as the
cohomology of the site, by `CategoryTheory.ProjectiveResolution.extAddEquivCohomologyClass`. -/
def chaoticDerivedGlobalSections : CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u} ℤ :=
  ((chaoticResolution X hX).cochainComplex).HomComplex
    ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor _ 0).obj F)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07JM.** Let `𝒞` carry the chaotic topology, let `X` be an object of
`𝒞` to which every object of `𝒞` admits a morphism, and let `𝒞` have products of pairs. For every
abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `𝒞` the total cohomology `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` is represented by the complex
`𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯` associated to the cosimplicial abelian group
`[n] ↦ 𝓕(X^{n + 1})`.

This is the comparison itself, an isomorphism of complexes of abelian groups between
`RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` and that complex placed in the nonnegative degrees. An isomorphism of complexes is
sent to an isomorphism of `D(Ab)` by the localisation functor, which is
`Stacks.Cohomology.derivedGlobalSectionsQIsoPowerCechComplexExtend`, and to the isomorphism of
cohomology groups in each degree, which is
`Stacks.Cohomology.sheafHAddEquivPowerCechComplexHomology`. -/
@[stacks 07JM]
def derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend :
    chaoticDerivedGlobalSections X hX F ≅
      (powerCechComplex F.obj X).extend ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat :=
  homComplexExtendIso X hX F ≪≫
    ((ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat.extendFunctor AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
      (powerCechComplexIso X F)).symm

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07JM**, in the derived category of abelian groups: on the chaotic site
with a covering object `X` and products of pairs, `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` and the complex
`𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯` become isomorphic in `D(Ab)`.

This is `Stacks.Cohomology.derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend` read through the
localisation functor `CategoryTheory.DerivedCategory.Q`. The instance
`HasDerivedCategory.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{u}` only chooses a model of `D(Ab)` with morphisms in a
given universe; one always exists, by `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`. -/
@[stacks 07JM]
def derivedGlobalSectionsQIsoPowerCechComplexExtend
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{u}] :
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj (chaoticDerivedGlobalSections X hX F) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((powerCechComplex F.obj X).extend ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend X hX F)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07JM** in degree `n`: the cohomology `H^n(𝒞, 𝓕)` of the chaotic site
is the degree-`n` cohomology of the complex `𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯`.

This is `H^n` of `Stacks.Cohomology.derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend`, the
cohomology of `RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` being `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H` by
`CategoryTheory.ProjectiveResolution.extAddEquivCohomologyClass`. It is the map whose existence
`Stacks.Cohomology.nonempty_addEquiv_sheafH_homology_powerCechComplex` asserts. -/
@[stacks 07JM]
def sheafHAddEquivPowerCechComplexHomology
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] (n : ℕ) :
    Sheaf.H F n ≃+ (powerCechComplex F.obj X).homology n :=
  (((chaoticResolution X hX).extAddEquivCohomologyClass (Y := F) (n := n)).trans
      (CochainComplex.HomComplex.homologyAddEquiv _ _ (n : ℤ)).symm).trans <|
    Iso.addCommGroupIsoToAddEquiv <|
      (HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℤ) (n : ℤ)).mapIso
          (derivedGlobalSectionsIsoPowerCechComplexExtend X hX F) ≪≫
        HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso (powerCechComplex F.obj X)
          ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (j := n) (j' := (n : ℤ)) rfl

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07JM** in degree `n`, as an isomorphism of objects of
`AddCommGrpCat`: the value at `𝓕` of Mathlib's cohomology functor `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.functorH`
of the chaotic site is the degree-`n` cohomology of the complex
`𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯`.

This is `Stacks.Cohomology.sheafHAddEquivPowerCechComplexHomology` read as a morphism of the
category `AddCommGrpCat`, which is the form in which an isomorphism of cohomology groups is
stated elsewhere in the library. -/
@[stacks 07JM]
def functorHObjIsoPowerCechComplexHomology
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] (n : ℕ) :
    (Sheaf.functorH (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) n).obj F ≅
      (powerCechComplex F.obj X).homology n :=
  (sheafHAddEquivPowerCechComplexHomology X hX F n).toAddCommGrpIso

include hX in
/-- **The comparison of [Stacks, Tag 07JM], named.** The isomorphism

`H^n(𝒞, 𝓕) ≅ H^n(𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → ⋯)`

that `Stacks.Cohomology.nonempty_addEquiv_sheafH_homology_powerCechComplex` asserts to exist, as
a `def`. It is the composite the tag's proof already writes down: the `Ext`-groups out of the
constant sheaf are the cohomology of the `Hom`-complex of the resolution
(`chaoticResolution`), that `Hom`-complex is the Čech complex extended by zero
(`homComplexExtendIso`), and extension by zero does not change the cohomology in the
nonnegative degrees.

A `Nonempty` of an isomorphism between two groups says nothing about any *given* map between
them, so every consumer that has to recognise a particular map as the comparison needs this
named form; see the degreewise statements of the crystalline chapter. -/
def addEquivSheafHHomologyPowerCechComplex
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] (n : ℕ) :
    Sheaf.H F n ≃+ (powerCechComplex F.obj X).homology n :=
  ((chaoticResolution X hX).extAddEquivCohomologyClass (Y := F) (n := n)).trans
    (((CochainComplex.HomComplex.homologyAddEquiv _ _ (n : ℤ)).symm).trans
      (Iso.addCommGroupIsoToAddEquiv
        ((HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℤ)
              (n : ℤ)).mapIso (homComplexExtendIso X hX F) ≪≫
          HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso (powerFreeCechComplex X F)
              ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (j := n) (j' := (n : ℤ)) rfl ≪≫
            (HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℕ) n).mapIso
              (powerCechComplexIso X F).symm)))

include hX in
/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07JM.** Let `𝒞` carry the chaotic topology, let `X` be an object of
`𝒞` to which every object of `𝒞` admits a morphism, and let the nonempty finite powers
`X^{n + 1}` of `X` exist in `𝒞`. For every abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `𝒞` the total cohomology
`RΓ(𝒞, 𝓕)` is represented by the complex `𝓕(X) → 𝓕(X × X) → 𝓕(X × X × X) → ⋯` associated to the
cosimplicial abelian group `[n] ↦ 𝓕(X^{n + 1})`: in every degree the cohomology of the site
agrees with the cohomology of that complex.

The source asks `𝒞` to have products of pairs; the hypothesis here is the weaker one that the
proof uses, and the source's implies it by `Stacks.Cohomology.hasProduct_fin_succ`.

The comparison itself is `Stacks.Cohomology.addEquivSheafHHomologyPowerCechComplex`; this is
that `def` read as an existence statement. -/
@[stacks 07JM]
theorem nonempty_addEquiv_sheafH_homology_powerCechComplex
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (⊥ : GrothendieckTopology C) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] (n : ℕ) :
    Nonempty (Sheaf.H F n ≃+ (powerCechComplex F.obj X).homology n) :=
  ⟨addEquivSheafHHomologyPowerCechComplex X hX F n⟩

end Main3

end Stacks.Cohomology

end
